      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part III, Line 1a: If organization elected under SFAS 116 to not report are, historical treasures, o</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION MAINTAINS THE TOMMIE CAMARILLO COLLECTION IN ADDITION TO PROVIDING A PLACE FOR ROTATING EXHIBITIONS AND A COMMUNITY ARTIST GALLERY:Tomasa is a self taught archivist and Chicano Park Steering Committee Chair Por Vida. Tomasa hosts her collection at the CPMCC so that it remains in the hands of the people. The collection relates to Chicano Park and the Chicano Movement, including: Chicano Park Day Posters, Audio tapes from numerous community meetings, Binders capturing the history of community struggles such as the fight for Bay Access, Community Newspapers, Video tapes of Chicano Park Day, Blueprints to numerous projects, and more. Through this partnership we seek to digitize and restore this collection to help preserve this history for the next generation of Chicanos and Chicanas.</ExplanationTxt>
